WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.413
Reinforcement learning has mastered complex skills,

00:00:03.493 --> 00:00:10.125
but almost always by assuming the environment
resets to a fixed initial state after every episode.

00:00:10.205 --> 00:00:14.919
In the real world, especially in robotics, those
resets are expensive,

00:00:14.999 --> 00:00:18.275
requiring human supervision or scripted routines.

00:00:18.355 --> 00:00:22.864
This work, presented at ICML 2023 by Jigang Kim,
Daesol Cho, and H.

00:00:22.944 --> 00:00:25.535
Jin Kim from Seoul National University,

00:00:25.615 --> 00:00:30.741
tackles autonomous reinforcement learning without
any resets and, crucially,

00:00:30.821 --> 00:00:32.590
without any demonstrations.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.302
Their method, called IBC,

00:00:34.382 --> 00:00:40.535
combines an auxiliary agent that fades away as the
main agent improves with a bidirectional

00:00:40.615 --> 00:00:43.480
goal curriculum built on optimal transport.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:48.274
The result is state-of-the-art performance on
non-episodic benchmarks,

00:00:48.354 --> 00:00:55.260
matching methods that rely on expert data and even
approaching episodic oracle reinforcement learning.
